{"article_ids": ["02d4f8f47ed9d027"], "canonical_title": "Beyond Outcome Gaps: Process-Aware Fairness Diagnosis for LLM-based Multi-Agent Decision Systems", "category": "research", "confidence": 0.93, "description": "Researchers introduced SCOPED-Hiring, a pipeline that creates controlled resume variants, runs role‑based hiring committees of large language models, and records over 311,000 structured decision‑trajectory logs to diagnose fairness throughout the hiring process rather than only at the outcome stage.", "entities": ["term:mas", "term:scoped"], "first_seen": "2026-09-03T04:00:00Z", "id": "evt_02d4f8f47ed9d027", "importance_score": 6.29, "last_updated": "2026-09-03T04:00:00Z", "source_ids": ["arxiv-cs-ai"]}
{"article_ids": ["563cfa9d420bb02c"], "canonical_title": "I rented a car, and within hours, my driver's license was for sale", "category": "security", "confidence": 0.6, "description": "A data breach is unfolding in real time, with personal information—including driver’s licenses—appearing for sale shortly after individuals rent cars. The FBI is reported to be investigating the breach.", "entities": ["term:fbi"], "first_seen": "2026-09-02T20:32:02Z", "id": "evt_563cfa9d420bb02c", "importance_score": 5.918, "last_updated": "2026-09-02T20:32:02Z", "source_ids": ["ars-technica"]}
{"article_ids": ["a6075ac6792b7e89", "33fbdf88b1a9548a"], "canonical_title": "Deterministic LLM Inference Across GPU Kernels: Power-of-Two INT8 Quantization Scales and the Limits of Tolerance-Based Conformance", "category": "research", "confidence": 0.9, "description": "Researchers applied an end‑to‑end post‑training conversion to the instruction‑tuned 4‑billion‑parameter Qwen model using KOTMS rotation, E2M‑ATQ ternarization, and GPTQ‑style error compensation. The process ternarizes the weights only, achieving an effective 1.58‑bit representation while keeping activations at 16‑bit precision.", "entities": ["model:qwen", "model:qwen-3", "term:atq", "term:gemm", "term:gptq", "term:kotms"], "first_seen": "2026-09-02T04:00:00Z", "id": "evt_a6075ac6792b7e89", "importance_score": 5.89, "last_updated": "2026-09-03T04:00:00Z", "source_ids": ["arxiv-cs-lg", "arxiv-cs-ai"]}
{"article_ids": ["355be2cf6d2d139c", "b56d9aff623d5523", "ef239918f16e1482", "fc8ba1244954cc96"], "canonical_title": "Introducing Gemini 3.8 Flash and 3.8 Flash Cyber", "category": "model_release", "confidence": 0.92, "description": "Google released the Gemini 3.8 Flash model a few weeks after Gemini 3.7 Flash, describing it as performing more reasoning steps and iteratively calling tools. The same introductory pricing as 3.7 Flash ($0.75 per million input tokens, $3.75 per million output tokens) is advertised. A variant called Gemini 3.8 Flash Cyber is also released but is only available to “trusted defenders.” The llm‑gemini 0.34 library added support for the new model with configurable low, medium, and high thinking levels and fixed an async‑response bug.", "entities": ["model:gemini", "model:gemini-0.34", "model:gemini-3", "model:gemini-3.7", "model:gemini-3.8", "org:google", "org:google-deepmind", "term:url"], "first_seen": "2026-09-02T15:12:40Z", "id": "evt_355be2cf6d2d139c", "importance_score": 5.65, "last_updated": "2026-09-02T20:11:40Z", "source_ids": ["google-deepmind", "the-verge-ai", "hacker-news", "simon-willison"]}
{"article_ids": ["262232089201014b"], "canonical_title": "WMLLM: Self-Evolving Optimization Agents via Predict-Then-Act World Modeling", "category": "research", "confidence": 0.7, "description": "The paper \"WMLLM: Self-Evolving Optimization Agents via Predict-Then-Act World Modeling\" (arXiv:2609.01608v1) proposes a new approach to black-box optimization. It uses large language models to build a predictive world model that suggests promising search directions before costly evaluations, employing a predict‑then‑act loop to improve sample efficiency in large, weakly structured, high‑dimensional spaces.", "entities": ["term:wmllm"], "first_seen": "2026-09-03T04:00:00Z", "id": "evt_262232089201014b", "importance_score": 5.64, "last_updated": "2026-09-03T04:00:00Z", "source_ids": ["arxiv-cs-lg"]}
